1 | go-backend | Remove every long dash character from the eight Go files the W1-B squash 5037176b touched, and change nothing else. House style bans U+2014, U+2013 and U+2015 in every generated file including code comments, and 39 of them reached main in that squash. THE FILES AND COUNTS, from git show 5037176b: apps/api/internal/config/config.go 6, apps/api/internal/config/config_test.go 2, apps/api/internal/handler/hermes_scope_enforcement_test.go 8, apps/api/internal/handler/routes.go 10, apps/api/internal/middleware/auth.go 7, apps/api/internal/middleware/auth_scope_test.go 4, apps/api/internal/model/concierge.go 1, apps/api/internal/service/auth.go 1. Only touch lines that squash ADDED; a long dash that was already on main before 5037176b is out of scope for this PR, so diff each file against 5037176b parent to know which lines are yours. For each occurrence, rewrite the sentence with a comma, a colon, parentheses or a new sentence, preserving meaning. Do not use a plain hyphen as a stand-in for an em dash in prose. Do not touch any string literal, test expectation or identifier; if a long dash sits inside a Go string literal that a test asserts on, STOP and report it rather than changing behaviour. VERIFY, real exit codes captured directly rather than read after a pipe: grep -rP for the three characters across the eight files must return zero; go build, go vet, the api unit suite with race, and golangci-lint must pass; and go test must show the SAME pass count as on main, since no test may change. Prove zero behaviour change mechanically: gofmt -l must be empty, and for each package, compile on main and on your branch and confirm the test binaries differ only in comment-derived positions, or state plainly if that comparison is not practical and rely on the test-count equality instead. Open a PR titled as a comment-only house-style fix referencing PR 2804 with Refs. No long dash in the commit or PR text, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Do not merge. | chore/strip-dashes-w1b

2 | backend-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the wave 1 change on branch chore/strip-dashes-w1b. No commits, no push, no review, no labels, no test writing. Permitted writes are a slash tmp worktree only. Record the PR head SHA at start and re-check at report; if it moved report BLOCKED with both SHAs. THE QUESTION THAT MATTERS: did anything other than comment text change. FIRST, run grep -rP for U+2014, U+2013 and U+2015 across the eight named files and confirm zero. SECOND, take the diff and confirm every changed line is a comment line: any hunk that touches code, a string literal, a test expectation or an identifier is a BLOCK, because this PR is sold as zero behaviour change. THIRD, confirm the test pass count on the branch equals main exactly, by running both. FOURTH, confirm gofmt -l is empty and go vet and golangci-lint pass. FIFTH, read a sample of the rewritten comments and confirm meaning was preserved rather than mangled; a comment that now says something different is a finding even though it compiles. SIXTH, no long dash, no vendor name in the commit or PR text. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC STRIP DASHES W1B, with SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX and file and line citations. No emails, booking ids or gcloud payloads. | chore/strip-dashes-w1b
